{
  "title": "Gate every request (podcast showcase)",
  "style": "podcast",
  "speakers": {
    "a": {
      "name": "Dana",
      "role": "Principal Security Engineer",
      "voice": "af_heart"
    },
    "b": {
      "name": "Omar",
      "role": "Principal Architect",
      "voice": "am_michael"
    }
  },
  "layout": "whiteboard",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01",
      "section": "hook",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Should every request go through the login service? I say yes. One missed check is a breach, and a breach costs far more than a few milliseconds.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "duo",
        "question": "Should every request go through the login service?",
        "quote": "One missed check is a breach."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "section": "setup",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "Hold on. Every request means one more network hop, and our budget is two hundred milliseconds in total.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "callout",
        "heading": "The budget",
        "big": "200 ms",
        "text": "Total time for one request"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "section": "exchange",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Then I stand by my claim: gate every request, no exceptions. A check that can be skipped is not a check.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "stance",
        "question": "Gate every request?",
        "entries": [
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Gate every request, no exceptions",
            "kind": "claim"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "section": "disagreement",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "And I disagree. One more hop blows the budget, and the budget is the product.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "stance",
        "question": "Gate every request?",
        "entries": [
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Gate every request, no exceptions",
            "kind": "claim"
          },
          {
            "by": "b",
            "text": "One more hop blows the budget",
            "kind": "disagree",
            "ref": 0
          }
        ]
      },
      "continues": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "section": "resolution",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Then verify at the edge. A signed token is checked in under a millisecond, so the extra hop disappears.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "stance",
        "question": "Gate every request?",
        "entries": [
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Gate every request, no exceptions",
            "kind": "claim"
          },
          {
            "by": "b",
            "text": "One more hop blows the budget",
            "kind": "disagree",
            "ref": 0
          },
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Verify at the edge, under a millisecond",
            "kind": "resolve",
            "ref": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      "continues": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "section": "disagreement",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "That leaves my real worry. Stale tokens outlive revoked accounts. How long does a fired contractor keep access?",
      "visual": {
        "type": "stance",
        "question": "Gate every request?",
        "entries": [
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Gate every request, no exceptions",
            "kind": "claim"
          },
          {
            "by": "b",
            "text": "One more hop blows the budget",
            "kind": "disagree",
            "ref": 0
          },
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Verify at the edge, under a millisecond",
            "kind": "resolve",
            "ref": 1
          },
          {
            "by": "b",
            "text": "Stale tokens outlive revoked accounts",
            "kind": "disagree",
            "ref": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      "continues": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "section": "resolution",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Five minute tokens, plus a deny list at the edge for revocation. The window stays short and the list stays small.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "stance",
        "question": "Gate every request?",
        "entries": [
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Gate every request, no exceptions",
            "kind": "claim"
          },
          {
            "by": "b",
            "text": "One more hop blows the budget",
            "kind": "disagree",
            "ref": 0
          },
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Verify at the edge, under a millisecond",
            "kind": "resolve",
            "ref": 1
          },
          {
            "by": "b",
            "text": "Stale tokens outlive revoked accounts",
            "kind": "disagree",
            "ref": 2
          },
          {
            "by": "a",
            "text": "Five minute tokens and a deny list",
            "kind": "resolve",
            "ref": 3
          }
        ]
      },
      "continues": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "section": "exchange",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "So the path changes. The client sends a token, the edge verifies it, and only then does the service do any work.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "flow",
        "heading": "Where the check happens",
        "nodes": [
          {
            "label": "Client",
            "sub": "sends a token"
          },
          {
            "label": "Edge check",
            "sub": "verifies it"
          },
          {
            "label": "Service",
            "sub": "does the work"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "section": "exchange",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Compare that with a session lookup on every call. It is simple and revocable at once, but it costs a database read each time.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "compare",
        "heading": "Two ways to check",
        "columns": [
          {
            "title": "Session lookup",
            "tag": "Database read",
            "items": [
              "Revoke at once",
              "One read per call",
              "Hard to scale"
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Signed token",
            "tag": "Edge check",
            "items": [
              "No lookup",
              "Short lived",
              "Deny list for revocation"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "section": "exchange",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "Writes are different. A stale token on a read leaks a page, but on a write it changes data. I want a full check there.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "steps",
        "heading": "What each call gets",
        "items": [
          "Read: edge check",
          "Write: full check",
          "Admin: full check and alert"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "section": "exchange",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Agreed, and that is the pivotal part. Fast reads, careful writes. The edge protects the budget and the full check protects the data.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "duo",
        "question": "Fast reads, careful writes",
        "quote": "The edge protects the budget."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "section": "exchange",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "One thing remains. We should measure the added latency after launch, so the next review has numbers instead of opinions.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "callout",
        "heading": "After launch",
        "big": "Measure it",
        "text": "Latency of the edge check"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "section": "close",
      "speaker": "a",
      "narration": "Let me close with what we agreed. Verify tokens at the edge, and keep tokens short lived, five minutes at most.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "notes",
        "heading": "Takeaways",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Verify tokens at the edge",
            "by": "a"
          },
          {
            "text": "Keep tokens short lived",
            "by": "b"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "section": "close",
      "speaker": "b",
      "narration": "And check every write in full. Then measure the latency after launch, so the decision rests on numbers.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "notes",
        "heading": "Takeaways",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Verify tokens at the edge",
            "by": "a"
          },
          {
            "text": "Keep tokens short lived",
            "by": "b"
          },
          {
            "text": "Check every write in full",
            "by": "b"
          },
          {
            "text": "Measure the latency"
          }
        ]
      },
      "continues": true
    }
  ]
}
